[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To configure LiveKit server:

1. Generate an API key/secret pair and put it under "keys:" in
   %%ETCDIR%%/livekit.yaml (readable by the %%LIVEKIT_USER%% user,
   e.g. chown root:%%LIVEKIT_GROUP%% and chmod 640):

     livekit-server generate-keys

   The sample config points at a Redis server ("redis:"). Redis is only
   needed for multi-node setups or with LiveKit Egress/Ingress; remove
   that section for a standalone node.

2. Open these ports in the firewall (defaults; see "livekit-server
   --config %%ETCDIR%%/livekit.yaml ports"):

     TCP 7880         HTTP/WebSocket signalling and API (put TLS in
                      front of it, e.g. a reverse proxy)
     UDP 50000-60000  WebRTC media (rtc.port_range_start/end)
     TCP 7881         WebRTC over TCP fallback (rtc.tcp_port)
     TURN, if enabled: turn.udp_port (UDP 3478) and turn.tls_port
     (TCP 5349)

   The service runs as %%LIVEKIT_USER%%, so ports below 1024 (e.g. TURN/TLS
   on 443) need mac_portacl(4) or net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedhigh.

3. A UDP receive buffer of at least 5 MB is recommended:

     sysctl kern.ipc.maxsockbuf=33554432

4. sysrc livekit_enable=YES && service livekit start

   Logs go to /var/log/livekit/livekit.log.
EOM
}
]
